My favourite rainbows aren't the big, showy ones that stretch across the whole sky. They're the little, secret rainbows you find in the most unexpected places.

Like the one that appears in the spray from the garden sprinkler on a sunny afternoon. It's tiny, just a shimmering arc of colour, but it's magical. Or the one you see when you hold a prism up to the light, and the white light splits into a miniature rainbow on the wall.

I love the way rainbows remind us that even after the rain, there's always beauty to be found. And that sometimes, the most beautiful things are the ones we have to look a little closer to see. [end of text]


